---
import GrammarModeSwitcher from "../../../../../components/GrammarModeSwitcher.astro";
import GrammarShell from "../../../../../components/GrammarShell.astro";

export const prerender = true;
const title = "Start Japanese Grammar From Zero — Jengo";
const description = "A short primer for absolute beginners before starting the Jengo Japanese grammar path.";
---

<GrammarShell title={title} description={description} canonical="https://jengolang.com/learn/japanese/grammar/path/start">
  <main class="grammar-wrap start-wrap">
    <a class="back" href="/learn/japanese/grammar/path">← Grammar path</a>
    <GrammarModeSwitcher mode="path" />

    <header class="page-head">
      <p>Start here</p>
      <h1>Before your first grammar unit.</h1>
      <div class="lede">This path teaches grammar. It assumes you can sound out hiragana and katakana, even slowly.</div>
    </header>

    <section class="readiness" aria-labelledby="readiness-title">
      <h2 id="readiness-title">Can you start?</h2>
      <p>If <span lang="ja">あ・か・さ</span> still looks unfamiliar, learn kana first. You do not need a large vocabulary or any grammar before returning here.</p>
      <a href="https://www.tofugu.com/japanese/learn-hiragana/">Learn hiragana and katakana →</a>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Three ideas to carry with you</p>
      <ol class="ideas">
        <li><strong>The important word usually comes last.</strong><span><span lang="ja">私は学生です。</span> means “I am a student.” The sentence ends with what it says about me.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Japanese often leaves out “I” and “you.”</strong><span>When the context makes the person clear, speakers do not repeat it.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Small words show a noun’s job.</strong><span>Words such as <span lang="ja">は</span>, <span lang="ja">が</span>, and <span lang="ja">を</span> tell you how a noun fits into the sentence. The first units build this carefully.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">The words used in early examples</p>
      <dl class="words">
        <div><dt lang="ja">私</dt><dd>watashi, I</dd></div>
        <div><dt lang="ja">これ / それ</dt><dd>this / that</dd></div>
        <div><dt lang="ja">誰 / 何 / どこ</dt><dd>who / what / where</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>You will also meet nouns (people and things), verbs (actions), and adjectives (descriptions). The first units name these as they become useful.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="labels-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Four labels you will see</p>
      <h2 id="labels-title">Know just enough terminology to keep going.</h2>
      <dl class="labels">
        <div><dt>Dictionary / plain form</dt><dd>A verb’s dictionary form is the form dictionaries list: <span lang="ja">食べる</span> “eat.” It is also the casual present/future form. A polite ending changes it to <span lang="ja">食べます</span>. Unit 3 makes this relationship concrete.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>i-adjective</dt><dd>A describing word ending in <span lang="ja">い</span>, such as <span lang="ja">高い</span> “expensive.”</dd></div>
        <div><dt>na-adjective</dt><dd>A describing word such as <span lang="ja">静か</span> “quiet.” It needs <span lang="ja">な</span> before a noun (<span lang="ja">静かな部屋</span>) but uses <span lang="ja">です</span> at the end of a polite sentence.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>You do not need to memorize every label now. They are signposts: they tell you which pattern a lesson is talking about.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="routine-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">When a page feels hard</p>
      <h2 id="routine-title">Use this reading routine.</h2>
      <ol class="routine">
        <li>Find the final word. It usually tells you what the sentence says.</li>
        <li>Find the particle after each noun. It tells you that noun’s job.</li>
        <li>If a page names a form, first ask “what shape is this?” Then ask “what does this shape let me say?”</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Follow the units in order at the beginning. A link to a later page is a preview, not a requirement to stop and learn it first.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="next" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ready</p>
      <h2 id="next-title">Make your first “X is Y” sentences.</h2>
      <p>Start with polite sentences, then learn how the plain form fits beside them.</p>
      <button id="mark-start" class="complete-start" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5"/></svg><span>Mark Unit 0 learned</span></button>
      <a class="primary" href="/learn/japanese/grammar/path#unit-1">Start Unit 1 →</a>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script type="module">
    function setupStart(){
    const progress=window.__jengoGrammarProgress;
    const root=document.querySelector(".start-wrap");
    if(!progress||!root||root.dataset.progressReady)return;
    root.dataset.progressReady="true";
    const {connectProgress,isLearned,loadProgress,saveProgress,setLearned}=progress;
    const slug="grammar-path-primer",button=document.querySelector("#mark-start");let state=loadProgress();
    const render=()=>{const on=isLearned(state,slug);button.setAttribute("aria-pressed",String(on));button.querySelector("span").textContent=on?"Unit 0 learned · tap to undo":"Mark Unit 0 learned"};
    button.addEventListener("click",()=>{setLearned(state,slug,!isLearned(state,slug));saveProgress(state,[slug]);render()});connectProgress((next)=>{state=next;render()});render();
    }
    document.addEventListener("astro:page-load",setupStart);
  </script>
</GrammarShell>

<style>
  .start-wrap{width:min(100% - 32px,720px)}.back{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:18px;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.back:hover{color:var(--brand)}.page-head{margin-top:30px}.page-head>p,.eyebrow{font-size:.7rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-tertiary)}h1{margin-top:4px;font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,3rem);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.03em}.lede{max-width:56ch;margin-top:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:1rem}.start-wrap section{margin-top:34px}.start-wrap h2{font-size:1.2rem;letter-spacing:-.015em}.start-wrap section>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:65ch;margin-top:8px;color:var(--text-secondary)}.readiness{padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;background:var(--brand-tint)}.readiness a{display:inline-block;margin-top:14px;color:var(--brand);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700}.ideas{display:grid;gap:18px;margin-top:14px;list-style:none;counter-reset:idea}.ideas li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:30px 1fr;gap:2px 12px;counter-increment:idea}.ideas li::before{content:counter(idea);grid-row:1/3;display:grid;place-items:center;width:27px;height:27px;border:1px solid var(--border-strong);border-radius:8px;color:var(--brand);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800}.ideas strong{font-size:.95rem}.ideas span{color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:.9rem}.ideas span[lang],.words dt,.labels dd span[lang]{font-family:"Noto Sans JP",sans-serif}.words,.labels{display:grid;gap:10px;margin-top:14px}.words div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:100px 1fr;gap:12px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.words dt{font-size:1rem;font-weight:700}.words dd,.labels dd{color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:.9rem}.labels div{padding-bottom:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.labels dt{font-size:.85rem;font-weight:800}.labels dd{margin-top:3px}.routine{display:grid;gap:10px;margin-top:14px;padding-left:21px;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:.9rem}.routine li::marker{color:var(--brand);font-weight:800}.next{padding-top:28px;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.next h2{margin-top:5px}.complete-start{width:100%;min-height:50px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:9px;margin-top:20px;border:1px solid color-mix(in oklab,var(--brand) 28%,var(--border));border-radius:10px;background:var(--brand-tint);color:var(--brand);font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}.complete-start svg{width:18px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.7;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.complete-start[aria-pressed="true"]{border-color:var(--learned);background:var(--learned);color:var(--white)}.primary{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;padding:11px 16px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--brand);color:var(--white);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.primary:hover{background:oklch(42% .089 156)}
</style>
